					<description><![CDATA[Kata ICON is a residential complex consisting of two fourteen-storey towers, built over a shared lobby at the entrance to the new Glil Yam neighbourhood in Herzliya. The site occupies land from the former kibbutz of the same name and is located next to a large green area, a position that led LSA Lazarovich Architects to conceive the project also as an urban intervention. “As an entrance project, we wanted to create a striking architectural presence that stood out from its surroundings while maintaining a respectful dialogue with neighbouring buildings,” explains Noy Lazarovich, head of the studio.]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p><img width="2000" height="1334" src="https://imgix.cosentino.com/usa/wp-content/uploads/Kata-Icon-Glil-Yam-4.jpg?auto=format%2Ccompress&amp;ixlib=php-3.3.0" class="attachment-full size-full wp-post-image wp-post-image" alt="Image 16 of Kata Icon Glil Yam 4.jpg?auto=format%2Ccompress&amp;ixlib=php 3.3 in {{Two fourteen-storey towers with Dekton on their façade}} - Cosentino" style="margin-bottom:20px;max-width:100%;height:auto" title="Image of Kata Icon Glil Yam 4.jpg?auto=format%2Ccompress&amp;ixlib=php 3.3 - Cosentino"></p>
