<div class="vc_row-full-width vc_clearfix"></div>
<section  data-vc-full-width="true" data-vc-full-width-init="false" class="vc_section">
<div class="container">
<div class="vc_row wpb_row vc_row-fluid mb-3 mb-none">
<div  class="wpb_column vc_column_container vc_col-sm-12">
<div class="vc_column-inner">
<div class="wpb_wrapper" style="" >
<div class=" wpb_text_column wpb_content_element " >
<div class="wpb_wrapper ">
<p>Kata ICON is a residential complex consisting of two fourteen-storey towers, built over a shared lobby at the entrance to the new Glil Yam neighbourhood in Herzliya. The site occupies land from the former kibbutz of the same name and is located next to a large green area, a position that led LSA Lazarovich Architects to conceive the project also as an urban intervention. “As an entrance project, we wanted to create a striking architectural presence that stood out from its surroundings while maintaining a respectful dialogue with neighbouring buildings,” explains Noy Lazarovich, head of the studio.</p>
</p></div>
</p></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="vc_row wpb_row vc_row-fluid mb-3 mb-none">
<div  class="wpb_column vc_column_container vc_col-sm-12">
<div class="vc_column-inner">
<div class="wpb_wrapper" style="" >
<div class="vc_empty_space"   style="height: 32px"><span class="vc_empty_space_inner"></span></div>
<div class="wpb_gallery wpb_content_element vc_clearfix wpb_content_element" >
<div class="wpb_wrapper">
<div class="wpb_gallery_slides wpb_flexslider flexslider_fade flexslider" data-interval="3" data-flex_fx="fade">
<ul class="slides">
<li><a class="" href="https://imgix.cosentino.com/usa/wp-content/uploads/Kata-Icon-Glil-Yam-4.jpg?auto=format%2Ccompress&#038;fit=crop&#038;ixlib=php-3.3.0&#038;max-h=734&#038;max-w=1100" data-lightbox="lightbox[rel-133167-3811546473]" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank"><img decoding="async" class="" src="https://imgix.cosentino.com/usa/wp-content/uploads/Kata-Icon-Glil-Yam-4-1110x740.jpg" width="1110" height="740" alt="Kata Icon Glil Yam (4)" title="Kata Icon Glil Yam (4)" /></a></li>
<li><a class="" href="https://imgix.cosentino.com/usa/wp-content/uploads/Kata-Icon-Glil-Yam-5.jpg?auto=format%2Ccompress&#038;fit=crop&#038;ixlib=php-3.3.0&#038;max-h=734&#038;max-w=1100" data-lightbox="lightbox[rel-133167-3811546473]" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank"><img decoding="async" class="" src="https://imgix.cosentino.com/usa/wp-content/uploads/Kata-Icon-Glil-Yam-5-1110x740.jpg" width="1110" height="740" alt="Kata Icon Glil Yam (5)" title="Kata Icon Glil Yam (5)" /></a></li>
</ul>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="vc_row wpb_row vc_row-fluid mb-3 mb-none">
<div  class="wpb_column vc_column_container vc_col-sm-12">
<div class="vc_column-inner">
<div class="wpb_wrapper" style="" >
<div class="vc_empty_space"   style="height: 32px"><span class="vc_empty_space_inner"></span></div>
<div class="vc_empty_space"   style="height: 32px"><span class="vc_empty_space_inner"></span></div>
<section  data-vc-full-width="true" data-vc-full-width-init="false" class="vc_section cos-title-subtitle cos-title-subtitle-6a82b9d76be11 vc_section-o-content-middle vc_section-flex">
<div class="container">
<div class="vc_row wpb_row vc_row-fluid">
<div  class="wpb_column vc_column_container">
<div class="vc_column-inner">
<div class="wpb_wrapper" style="" >
<h3  class="" style="color:; text-align:">A calling card</h3>
</p></div>
</div>
</div></div>
</p></div>
</section>
<div class="vc_row-full-width vc_clearfix"></div>
</p></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="vc_row wpb_row vc_row-fluid mb-3 mb-none">
<div  class="wpb_column vc_column_container vc_col-sm-8">
<div class="vc_column-inner">
<div class="wpb_wrapper" style="" >
<div class=" wpb_text_column wpb_content_element " >
<div class="wpb_wrapper ">
<p>With this commission, the developer aimed to create a high-end residential complex that would serve as the calling card for the new neighbourhood, both through its image and the urban experience associated with it. The programme included spacious homes oriented towards the nearby park and the sea, visible from the upper floors, as well as communal spaces designed to reinforce the project's identity. The approved scheme allowed for ten-storey buildings with six homes per level, a configuration that, according to Lazarovich, created “a kind of wall effect” that weakened the relationship with the street and public space.</p>
</p></div>
</p></div>
<div class=" wpb_text_column wpb_content_element " >
<div class="wpb_wrapper ">
<p>"The challenge was to promote a change that would allow for increased height in exchange for reducing ground occupation, improving the quality of the homes, freeing up space for the public square, and creating an open and welcoming place at the entrance to the neighbourhood,” explains the architect. The approval of this modification allowed the complex to acquire a broader urban dimension and become part of the everyday life of the surroundings.</p>
</p></div>
</p></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div  class="wpb_column vc_column_container vc_col-sm-4">
<div class="vc_column-inner">
<div class="wpb_wrapper" style="" >
<div class=" wpb_text_column wpb_content_element " >
<div class="wpb_wrapper ">
<p>The same idea is also reflected in the composition of the façades. The studio employed a language of balanced proportions that enhances the verticality of the towers and highlights the presence of the complex within the new residential development. “The project adopts a modern and refined architectural language that conveys elegance and a sense of understated luxury while maintaining harmony with the surroundings,” notes Lazarovich. “The façades are defined by precise lines and carefully selected materials, with special attention to proportions.”</p>
</p></div>
</p></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="vc_row wpb_row vc_row-fluid mb-3 mb-none">
<div  class="wpb_column vc_column_container vc_col-sm-12">
<div class="vc_column-inner">
<div class="wpb_wrapper" style="" >
<div class="vc_empty_space"   style="height: 32px"><span class="vc_empty_space_inner"></span></div>
<div class="wpb_gallery wpb_content_element vc_clearfix wpb_content_element" >
<div class="wpb_wrapper">
<div class="wpb_gallery_slides wpb_flexslider flexslider_fade flexslider" data-interval="3" data-flex_fx="fade">
<ul class="slides">
<li><a class="" href="https://imgix.cosentino.com/usa/wp-content/uploads/Kata-Icon-Glil-Yam-1.jpg?auto=format%2Ccompress&#038;fit=crop&#038;ixlib=php-3.3.0&#038;max-h=734&#038;max-w=1100" data-lightbox="lightbox[rel-133167-314634384]" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank"><img decoding="async" class="" src="https://imgix.cosentino.com/usa/wp-content/uploads/Kata-Icon-Glil-Yam-1-1110x740.jpg" width="1110" height="740" alt="Kata Icon Glil Yam (1)" title="Kata Icon Glil Yam (1)" /></a></li>
<li><a class="" href="https://imgix.cosentino.com/usa/wp-content/uploads/Kata-Icon-Glil-Yam-2.jpg?auto=format%2Ccompress&#038;fit=crop&#038;ixlib=php-3.3.0&#038;max-h=733&#038;max-w=1100" data-lightbox="lightbox[rel-133167-314634384]" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank"><img decoding="async" class="" src="https://imgix.cosentino.com/usa/wp-content/uploads/Kata-Icon-Glil-Yam-2-1110x740.jpg" width="1110" height="740" alt="Kata Icon Glil Yam (2)" title="Kata Icon Glil Yam (2)" /></a></li>
</ul>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="vc_row wpb_row vc_row-fluid mb-3 mb-none">
<div  class="wpb_column vc_column_container vc_col-sm-12">
<div class="vc_column-inner">
<div class="wpb_wrapper" style="" >
<div class="vc_empty_space"   style="height: 32px"><span class="vc_empty_space_inner"></span></div>
<div class="vc_empty_space"   style="height: 32px"><span class="vc_empty_space_inner"></span></div>
<section  data-vc-full-width="true" data-vc-full-width-init="false" class="vc_section cos-title-subtitle cos-title-subtitle-6a82b9d76be11 vc_section-o-content-middle vc_section-flex">
<div class="container">
<div class="vc_row wpb_row vc_row-fluid">
<div  class="wpb_column vc_column_container">
<div class="vc_column-inner">
<div class="wpb_wrapper" style="" >
<h3  class="" style="color:; text-align:">Preserving the continuity of the towers</h3>
</p></div>
</div>
</div></div>
</p></div>
</section>
<div class="vc_row-full-width vc_clearfix"></div>
</p></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="vc_row wpb_row vc_row-fluid mb-3 mb-none">
<div  class="wpb_column vc_column_container vc_col-sm-12">
<div class="vc_column-inner">
<div class="wpb_wrapper" style="" >
<div class=" wpb_text_column wpb_content_element " >
<div class="wpb_wrapper ">
<p>"We were looking for finishing materials capable of meeting the highest standards in terms of design, durability, and architectural clarity," explains Lazarovich. "Dekton surfaces perfectly fit that purpose thanks to their strong visual presence, long-term resistance, and the ability to clad façades with large-format pieces, reducing the number of cuts and preserving a continuous image. Dekton met all our expectations."</p>
</p></div>
</p></div>
<div class=" wpb_text_column wpb_content_element " >
<div class="wpb_wrapper ">
<p>The envelope incorporates a ventilated façade made with Dekton Moone and Dekton Micron. The studio sought a surface capable of preserving the visual continuity of the elevations through large-format pieces installed at full height while also meeting the specific conditions of an exterior application. Dekton's mechanical properties, along with its resistance to ultraviolet rays and freeze-thaw cycles, ensure its performance under continuous exposure. Its resistance to abrasion and stains facilitates façade maintenance, while its non-combustible nature provides additional assurance for the building envelope. Cosentino offers a 25-year warranty for this application and supports the product with the Carbon Neutral seal, tied to the company's sustainability commitment.</p>
</p></div>
</p></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="vc_row wpb_row vc_row-fluid mb-3 mb-none">
<div  class="wpb_column vc_column_container vc_col-sm-12">
<div class="vc_column-inner">
<div class="wpb_wrapper" style="" >
<div class="vc_empty_space"   style="height: 32px"><span class="vc_empty_space_inner"></span></div>
<div class="wpb_gallery wpb_content_element vc_clearfix wpb_content_element" >
<div class="wpb_wrapper">
<div class="wpb_gallery_slides wpb_flexslider flexslider_fade flexslider" data-interval="3" data-flex_fx="fade">
<ul class="slides">
<li><a class="" href="https://imgix.cosentino.com/usa/wp-content/uploads/Kata-Icon-Glil-Yam-3.jpg?auto=format%2Ccompress&#038;fit=crop&#038;ixlib=php-3.3.0&#038;max-h=734&#038;max-w=1100" data-lightbox="lightbox[rel-133167-3712926591]" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank"><img decoding="async" class="" src="https://imgix.cosentino.com/usa/wp-content/uploads/Kata-Icon-Glil-Yam-3-1110x740.jpg" width="1110" height="740" alt="Kata Icon Glil Yam (3)" title="Kata Icon Glil Yam (3)" /></a></li>
</ul>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
