					<description><![CDATA[The light stripe structure and filled pores of Dekton Marmorio are inspired by Navona travertine, a natural stone quarried near Tivoli, east of Rome. This aesthetic was precisely what Miall Architecture was looking for in a house in Williamstown, a historic coastal neighbourhood located southwest of Melbourne's centre. “I wanted to use travertine throughout the project, but we needed a very durable and practical material for a family home. Dekton allowed us to achieve the look of natural stone without its drawbacks,” the studio recalls.]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p><img width="2000" height="1334" src="https://imgix.cosentino.com/usa/wp-content/uploads/Williamtown-4.jpg?auto=format%2Ccompress&amp;ixlib=php-3.3.0" class="attachment-full size-full wp-post-image wp-post-image" alt="Image 32 of Williamtown 4.jpg?auto=format%2Ccompress&amp;ixlib=php 3.3 in {{The beauty of travertine with Dekton Marmorio brings continuity to this elegant home}} - Cosentino" style="margin-bottom:20px;max-width:100%;height:auto" title="Image of Williamtown 4.jpg?auto=format%2Ccompress&amp;ixlib=php 3.3 - Cosentino"></p>
<div class="wpb-content-wrapper">
<section style="position: relative; background:#ffffff" data-vc-full-width="true" data-vc-full-width-init="false" class="vc_section vc_custom_1596523778098 cos-section">
<div class='cos-cut-background cos-cut-height-11-12' style='background-color: #d9dedf'></div>
<div class="container">
