<section  data-vc-full-width="true" data-vc-full-width-init="false" class="vc_section cos-title-subtitle cos-title-subtitle-6a82b9d76be11 vc_section-o-content-middle vc_section-flex">
<div class="container">
<div class="vc_row wpb_row vc_row-fluid">
<div  class="wpb_column vc_column_container">
<div class="vc_column-inner">
<div class="wpb_wrapper" style="" >
<h3  class="" style="color:; text-align:">A collection designed as a system</h3>
</p></div>
</div>
</div></div>
</p></div>
</section>
<div class="vc_row-full-width vc_clearfix"></div>
</p></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="vc_row wpb_row vc_row-fluid mb-3 mb-none">
<div  class="wpb_column vc_column_container vc_col-sm-12">
<div class="vc_column-inner">
<div class="wpb_wrapper" style="" >
<div class=" wpb_text_column wpb_content_element " >
<div class="wpb_wrapper ">
<p>In Patricia Urquiola's constant quest for balance, Silestone surfaces act as a unifying element, providing visual continuity, durability, and a unique materiality.</p>
</p></div>
</p></div>
<div class=" wpb_text_column wpb_content_element " >
<div class="wpb_wrapper ">
<p>Rather than designing independent pieces, Urquiola has created a language that repeats at different scales. The interplay between two planes also appears in freestanding bathtubs, where an oval edge seems to rest on a continuous base, creating a light and highly recognisable silhouette. Auxiliary furniture alternates closed storage with perfectly proportioned open shelves, while suspended sanitary ware maintains the same refined geometry that defines the entire collection. Even the taps contribute to this quest for coherence with soft cylindrical shapes.</p>
</p></div>
</p></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="vc_row wpb_row vc_row-fluid mb-3 mb-none">
