		<item>
		<title>{{Dekton redefines the image of Lighthaus, a residential tower in Liverpool&#8217;s historic docks}}</title>
		<link>https://www.cosentino.com/usa/blog/dekton-redefines-the-image-of-lighthaus-a-residential-tower-in-liverpools-historic-docks/</link>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[sarabarragan]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Tue, 04 Aug 2026 10:10:45 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[{{Blog & Events}}]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Cladding]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Countertop]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Dekton]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Facade]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Kitchen]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.cosentino.com/usa/?p=133071</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[Thirty-one floors elevate Lighthaus Liverpool above Princes Dock, one of the areas included in the Liverpool Waters regeneration. The building, designed by Falconer Chester Hall, houses 278 rental apartments and dedicates the communal floors to shared services, with a 24-hour reception and spaces designed for resident interaction. Its location next to the Mersey required addressing the envelope to withstand continuous exposure to wind and saline conditions.]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p><img width="2000" height="1333" src="https://imgix.cosentino.com/usa/wp-content/uploads/Lighthouse-Liverpool-24.jpg?auto=format%2Ccompress&amp;ixlib=php-3.3.0" class="attachment-full size-full wp-post-image wp-post-image" alt="Image 142 of Lighthouse Liverpool 24.jpg?auto=format%2Ccompress&amp;ixlib=php 3.3 in {{Dekton redefines the image of Lighthaus, a residential tower in Liverpool&#039;s historic docks}} - Cosentino" style="margin-bottom:20px;max-width:100%;height:auto" title="Image of Lighthouse Liverpool 24.jpg?auto=format%2Ccompress&amp;ixlib=php 3.3 - Cosentino"></p>
<div class="wpb-content-wrapper">
