<div class=" wpb_text_column wpb_content_element " >
<div class="wpb_wrapper ">
<p>Thirty-one floors elevate Lighthaus Liverpool above Princes Dock, one of the areas included in the Liverpool Waters regeneration. The building, designed by Falconer Chester Hall, houses 278 rental apartments and dedicates the communal floors to shared services, with a 24-hour reception and spaces designed for resident interaction. Its location next to the Mersey required addressing the envelope to withstand continuous exposure to wind and saline conditions.</p>
</p></div>
</p></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div  class="wpb_column vc_column_container vc_col-sm-6">
<div class="vc_column-inner">
<div class="wpb_wrapper" style="" >
<div class=" wpb_text_column wpb_content_element " >
<div class="wpb_wrapper ">
<p>The façade combines a triple-glazed curtain wall with vertical elements running along the tower and opaque panels on the lower volume. The glass system incorporates solar control and ventilation panels. Falconer Chester Hall drew inspiration from Liverpool's maritime past and the port nature of Princes Dock to define the building's composition, with the base gaining prominence through the treatment of the podium.</p>
</p></div>
</p></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="vc_row wpb_row vc_row-fluid mb-3 mb-none">
<div  class="wpb_column vc_column_container vc_col-sm-12">
<div class="vc_column-inner">
<div class="wpb_wrapper" style="" >
<div class="vc_empty_space"   style="height: 32px"><span class="vc_empty_space_inner"></span></div>
